3	//! Registered as a web browser on Windows, UniMail receives every link the system opens. A Google
4	//! sign-in link becomes an account picker in the app; every other link is forwarded, untouched, to
5	//! the browser the user actually uses. That's how "Sign in with Google" from any site or app lands
6	//! on UniMail's accounts instead of whatever the default browser happens to be logged into.
