1	//! Per-account Google sessions.
2	//!
3	//! WebView2 allows only one user-data folder per process, so every account's Google window runs
4	//! in its own helper process (`unimail.exe --google <id> <email> [url]`) with its own cookie jar.
5	//! That gives each account a fully separate, persistent Google login, independent of every other
6	//! account and of the user's own browser.
7	//!
8	//! The helper does two things:
9	//!   1. Shows Google in that profile (app-passwords page by default, or a site's OAuth URL).
10	//!   2. Bounces the site's OAuth callback to the user's real browser and exits, so the site
11	//!      session lands where the user actually browses.
12	
